{"obsah":"<p>Split into 3 teams, we covered a large part of our beautiful country. Martin Šimůnek headed to Ralsko, where several tens of thousands of visitors gather at the mega event Forestry Day to check out the machinery and everything connected with the forest. It also includes a rich side programme, which traditionally includes an exhibition by Martin and our team.</p>\n\n<p><br>Michal Budský and Lukáš Valný, on the other hand, crossed the whole country to Hranice, where Cement Hranice was celebrating a respectable 70 years since its founding. It had one big advantage – the obstacles were already prepared on site, so the guys got to ride on concrete blocks and bags of cement.</p>\n\n<p><br>Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček and Mára Tryner went to Chocenice near Plzeň with our Kabeláč kids' selection, jumping at a small village festival. Everyone has a technical problem sometimes, and this time it was us – or rather Mára Tryner, whose chain tensioner spring snapped. Luckily a spring was found on Nikolka Kabeláčová's bike, and she took on the role of photographer. Judging by the feedback the event went great, and the beautiful weather helped bring in a big turnout.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F06%2F448343411_2288578471503637_664270366737896870_n.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F06%2F448343411_2288578471503637_664270366737896870_n.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-247727\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F06%2FIMG_6893.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bik